  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed at The Wilbury in Tallahassee, FL, on August 31, 2018, marking the 263rd show in the archive’s collection for the band [3]. This recording is the most complete available, capturing 30 songs over 90 minutes, compared to a 21-song alternative upload [1][2]. The setlist includes a notable solo section where John played “Waco,” “The Plague,” and “Cut Off Their Thumbs” [1][2]. “Waco” and “The Plague” were bustouts, not appearing in the preceding 214 and 231 archived shows, respectively [1]. “Cut Off Their Thumbs” was a mythic rare, with only two archived performances total [1]. The full band returned for “In Memory of Satan” and “The Diaz Brothers” [1][2]. The encore featured “See America Right,” “This Year,” “No Children,” and “Up the Wolves” [1][2]. The uploader described the atmosphere as one of the most intimate shows they had attended, highlighting incredible crowd energy [1]. Al Riggs opened the tour leg, and his performance is also worth listening to [1]. This recording was taped and transferred by ezralite23 [2].",
